Default:
  $_STRICT_DIG_OPTIONS

Notes:
  - This is most relevant when _BINARY=auto.
  - Does not affect runs where binary resolves to dig.

See also:
  --help dig-options
  --help binary
EOF

            ;;
        batch)

            help_topic_header "batch"

            cat <<EOF
Meaning:
  Enables dig query batching and sets batch size.

Flag:
  --batch N
  --batch=N

Equivalent environment effects:
  _DIG_BATCH=1
  _DIG_BATCH_SIZE=N

Scope:
  dig only. If binary resolves to nslookup, batching is disabled with warning.

Effective size:
  _DIG_BATCH_SIZE_EFFECTIVE = min(_DIG_BATCH_SIZE, _BURST), at least 1.
  In parallel mirrored fanout, logical batch admissions are:
  floor(_DIG_BATCH_SIZE_EFFECTIVE / endpoint_count), at least 1.

See also:
  --help burst
  --help dig-options
  --help runtime
  --help environment
EOF

            ;;
        burst)

            help_topic_header "burst"

            cat <<EOF
Meaning:
  Max burst size for token bucket (max dispatches per scheduler tick).

Default:
  $_BURST

Validation: positive integer.

Burst behaviour:
  - Clamped to (_QPS * 2) by default
  - When tokens available, dispatch up to _BURST queries immediately
  - Use --force-burst or append '!' to override safety clamp

Runtime clamp applies: _BURST is capped at (_QPS * 2).
Override with -B N! or --force-burst --burst N.

See also:
  --help force-burst
  --help batch
  --help auto-tune

Note:
  Burst controls dispatch pacing; worker count remains fixed at -m/--maximum.
  When --batch is enabled for dig, burst still caps admitted queries per tick,
  while batch size controls queries per dig process.
EOF

            ;;
        force-burst)

            help_topic_header "force-burst"

            cat <<EOF
Meaning:
  Overrides the burst safety clamp tied to _QPS (default: _BURST <= _QPS * 2).

Usage:
  -B 200!
  --force-burst --burst 200

Effect:
  Allows higher burst admission than the default safety clamp.

See also:
  --help burst
  --help qps
  --help auto-tune
EOF

            ;;
        column)

            help_topic_header "column"

            cat <<EOF
Meaning:
  CSV column index when reading file/url source.

Default:
  $_COLUMN

0 means auto-detect.

Validation:
  Non-negative integer.
EOF

            ;;
        custom)

            help_topic_header "custom"

            cat <<EOF
Meaning:
  Custom domain file prepended to primary source before dedupe/top-N.

Default:
  $_CUSTOM
EOF

            ;;
        directory)

            help_topic_header "directory"

            cat <<EOF
Meaning:
  Cache/work directory for downloaded sources and cache files.

Default:
  $_DIRECTORY
EOF

            ;;
        duration)

            help_topic_header "duration"

            cat <<EOF
Meaning:
  Runtime length in seconds.

Default:
  $_DURATION

0 = continuous loop.

Note:
  Also accepts plain seconds or human-readable duration (e.g. 1d 2h 3m 4s).

Timer guard:
  Under ${UNIT_BASE}.service + ${UNIT_BASE}.timer, _DURATION may be clamped
  to the detected timer period to avoid overlap.
  Optional override for period detection: _TIMER_PERIOD (duration syntax).

See also:
  --help runtime
  --help seconds
  --help clock-tick-ms
  --help drain-timeout-ms
EOF

            ;;
        file)

            help_topic_header "file"

            cat <<EOF
Meaning:
  Use local input file; overrides URL download path.

Default:
  (empty)

Must be readable.
EOF

            ;;
        format)

            help_topic_header "format"

            cat <<EOF
Values:
  auto | plain | csv

Default:
  $_FORMAT

Note:
  Domain validation is pragmatic (not full RFC/IDN validation).
EOF

            ;;
        local)

            help_topic_header "local"

            cat <<EOF
Meaning:
  Local resolver address.

Accepted:
  IPv4/IPv6, optional #port or [ipv6]:port.

Default:
  $_LOCAL

Behaviour:
  Sets the local resolver target. If --location is not explicitly set,
  this also makes local the active location.

See also:
  --help resolver
  --help location
  --help remote
EOF

            ;;
        location)

            help_topic_header "location"

            cat <<EOF
Values:
  auto | local | remote

Default:
  $_LOCATION

Meaning:
  Selects resolver location mode.

Modes:
  auto    best-effort default path
  local   force local mode (override for advanced testing)
  remote  force remote mode (override for advanced testing)

Use case:
  Allows deliberate local/remote classification overrides in spoofed or
  lab/test network scenarios.

See also:
  --help resolver
  --help local
  --help remote
EOF

            ;;
        maximum)

            help_topic_header "maximum"

            cat <<EOF
Meaning:
  Max concurrent query workers.

Default:
  $_MAXIMUM

Validation:
  Positive integer, clamped to 128.

Note:
  By default, the maximum worker count is clamped to 128 to prevent runaway
  resource usage. To override, append '!' to the value (e.g. -m 200!) or use
  --force-maximum together with -m/--maximum (e.g. -m 500 --force-maximum).

See also:
  --help force-maximum
  --help auto-tune
  --help burst
EOF

            ;;
        force-maximum)

            help_topic_header "force-maximum"

            cat <<EOF
Meaning:
  Overrides the clamp on maximum worker count when used with -m/--maximum.

Usage:
  -m 200!
  --maximum 200 --force-maximum

See also:
  --help maximum
  --help auto-tune
EOF

            ;;
        output)

            help_topic_header "output"

            cat <<EOF
Values:
  quiet | answer

Default:
  $_OUTPUT

quiet suppresses answer output; answer prints response records.
EOF

            ;;
        port)

            help_topic_header "port"

            cat <<EOF
Meaning:
  DNS service port used by query tool.

Default:
  $_PORT

Range:
  1..65535.
EOF

            ;;
        qps)

            help_topic_header "qps"

            cat <<EOF
Meaning:
  Token refill rate (queries/sec target).

Default:
  $_QPS

Validation:
  Positive integer.

Parallel mirrored fanout:
  Global backend QPS is still governed by _QPS.
  Each logical domain admission in parallel consumes one token per endpoint.
  This preserves global backend budget while mirroring domains to all
  resolvers.

See also:
  --help burst
  --help maximum
  --help auto-tune
  --help runtime
EOF

            ;;
        clock-tick-ms)

            help_topic_header "clock-tick-ms"

            cat <<EOF
Meaning:
  Scheduler sleep/check tick cap in milliseconds (environment variable only).

Variable:
  _CLOCK_TICK_MS

Default:
  $_CLOCK_TICK_MS

Validation:
  Positive integer.

Guidance:
  Lower = smoother pacing, more timing overhead.
  Higher = less timing overhead, burstier pacing (try 10-20ms).
EOF

            ;;
        drain-timeout-ms)

            help_topic_header "drain-timeout-ms"

            cat <<EOF
Meaning:
  Max time (ms) to wait for graceful worker drain after duration-based stop.

Variable:
  _DRAIN_TIMEOUT_MS

Default:
  $_DRAIN_TIMEOUT_MS

Validation:
  Non-negative integer.

Behaviour:
  - On duration stop: graceful drain waits up to this timeout, then force-stops workers.
  - On EOF/normal source exhaustion: default graceful stop path remains unchanged.
  - On abort signal: force cleanup path is used immediately.

Guidance:
  Use lower values for faster exit after timed runs.
EOF

            ;;
        random)

            help_topic_header "random"

            cat <<EOF
Meaning:
  Enables per-query RR type randomization from a built-in common pool.

Pool:
  A AAAA CNAME MX NS TXT

Default:
  $_RANDOM (0=off, 1=on)

Behaviour:
  When enabled, DNdistresS picks one RR type from the pool for each
  queued query before handing work to workers. This makes mixed query
  traffic look more organic than a single fixed RR type.

Note:
  --random and -T/--type are mutually exclusive.
  Use _RANDOM_RR_POOL to control random-mode RR types.
EOF

            ;;
        remote)

            help_topic_header "remote"

            cat <<EOF
Meaning:
  Remote resolver address.

Accepted:
  IPv4/IPv6, optional #port or [ipv6]:port.

Default:
  $_REMOTE

Behaviour:
  Sets the remote resolver target. If --location is not explicitly set,
  this also makes remote the active location.

See also:
  --help resolver
  --help location
  --help local
EOF

            ;;
        seconds)

            help_topic_header "seconds"

            cat <<EOF
Meaning:
  Cache TTL for downloaded source.

Default:
  $_SECONDS

0 disables cache.

Note:
  Also accepts plain seconds or human-readable duration (e.g. 5d 6h 7m 8s).

See also:
  --help directory
  --help url
  --help file
EOF

            ;;
        top)

            help_topic_header "top"

            cat <<EOF
Meaning:
  Keep top N domains after deduplication, optionally filtered by one or more
  patterns. Multiple patterns are OR-matched; a domain passes if any pattern
  matches.

Pattern forms:
  .com          suffix match  (domain ends with .com)
  ^google       prefix match  (domain starts with google)
  google        substring match
  ||google.com  adblock anchor (matches google.com and *.google.com)
  /regex/       POSIX awk extended regex

Usage:
  -t (N|PATTERN)...

Examples:
  -t 5000
  -t 5000 .com
  -t 5000 .com .net .org
  -t 1000 ||google.com
  -t 2000 /\\.gov\\.au\$/
  -t 5000 ^google ^facebook
  -t .co.nz 1000

Default count:
  $_TOP

Default filters:
  (none)

Validation:
  Count is a positive integer; patterns are matched in order.
EOF

            ;;
        type)

            help_topic_header "type"

            cat <<EOF
Meaning:
  DNS RR type for dig/nslookup (A, MX, AAAA, TXT, etc).

Default:
  $_TYPE

Also accepted:
  Numeric RR type IDs (examples: 1, 15, 28, 65, etc).

Recognised types:
  A          1
  NS         2
  CNAME      5
  SOA        6
  PTR        12
  MX         15
  TXT        16
  AAAA       28
  SRV        33
  NAPTR      35
  DNAME      39
  DS         43
  SSHFP      44
  IPSECKEY   45
  RRSIG      46
  NSEC       47
  DNSKEY     48
  NSEC3      50
  NSEC3PARAM 51
  TLSA       52
  CDS        59
  CDNSKEY    60
  OPENPGPKEY 61
  CSYNC      62
  ZONEMD     63
  SVCB       64
  HTTPS      65
  EUI48      108
  EUI64      109
  ANY        255
  CAA        257

Note:
  ANY (including ID 255) is rejected by default (--deny-any).
  Use --allow-any to permit it.

See also:
  --help random
  --help deny-any
  --help allow-any
EOF

            ;;
        deny-any|allow-any)

